  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral upper respiratory infection (common cold) (J06.9)</content>. Day three of a typical cold, with cough and rhinorrhea pointing to a virus. Temperature 37.6 °C, heart rate 86, and a clear chest, so pneumonia is not suspected. Antibiotics, a strep test, and a chest radiograph are not indicated. [S]<list><item>Honey for the cough, warm fluids, saline nasal rinse, and rest.</item><item>Acetaminophen or ibuprofen as needed for sore throat or fever, at label doses.</item><item>Repeat the home COVID-19 antigen test in 48 hours and call if it is positive.</item><item>The cough may last two to three weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic insomnia, disrupted by the cold (G47.00)</content>. Cough and nasal blockage are waking him, and the over-the-counter products he considered would work against his sleep plan. [S]<list><item>Avoid &quot;nighttime&quot; cold products containing diphenhydramine or doxylamine: sedating antihistamines are not recommended as sleep aids, leave next-day grogginess, and would undo the plan of sleeping without sedatives.</item><item>Avoid oral decongestants such as pseudoephedrine and phenylephrine, especially after midday, because they can worsen insomnia, raise blood pressure, and bring on a racing heart and jitteriness that can feel like his old hyperarousal.</item><item>Avoid alcohol-containing cough syrups.</item><item>Saline rinse before bed and the head of the bed raised; honey for night-time cough.</item><item>Keep the fixed wake time, and if awake for more than about 20 minutes, get up until sleepy, as in his routine.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-traumatic stress disorder, much improved (F43.10)</content>. Stable through the illness: nightmares not increased and no suicidal thoughts on a brief check. The safety plan remains in place. [S]<list><item>Continue the therapy skills and the safety plan.</item><item>Adult preventive visit later this month as booked.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Chronic Insomnia Disorder and Obstructive Sleep Apnea (2025); Appropriate Antibiotic Use for Acute Respiratory Tract Infection in Adults: Advice for High-Value Care From the American College of Physicians and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (2016)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Call or return for a temperature of 38.5 °C or higher, breathlessness, chest pain, facial or ear pain, symptoms lasting beyond ten days, or worsening after initial improvement. Adult preventive visit later this month as booked. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-27: adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
